Info: 
Usage: openETPServer [global-options] probe --info -S URL
Usage: openETPServer [global-options] probe --ping -S URL [auth-options]

Actions:
  -h [ --help ]                        Display this information
  --info                               Get ETP 1.2 server capabilities
  --ping                               Connect and ping ETP 1.2 server
  --osdu                               Get OSDU data platform support info

Connect Options:
  -S [ --server-url ] arg              ETP 1.2 server URL
  --etp-trace arg                      Trace ETP messages to file
                                       Filename inferred if empty or directory
  --timeout arg (=10s,10s)             ETP timeouts for CONNECT and GET/PUT 
                                       requests
  -M [ --max-msg-size ] arg (=1MB)     Maximum WebSocket message size(s) in 
                                       bytes
  -B [ --max-batch-size ] arg (=100)   Maximum parts per multi-part message
  -Q [ --msg-queue-depth ] arg (=500)  Deprecated: Maximum concurrent 
                                       (in-flight) messages
  --acknowledge                        Set Acknowledge flag on all ETP requests
  -Z [ --compress ] [=arg(=gzip)]      Set Compress-Body flag on all ETP 
                                       requests
                                       Specify compressor(s) (Default: gzip)
  --shun-protocols arg                 Force client to ignore those protocols

Authentication Options:
  -A [ --auth ] arg (=auto)            Authentication method: 'auto, 'none', 
                                       'basic', 'bearer'.
  -u [ --username ] arg                User's name to authenticate with.
  -p [ --password ] arg                User's password to authenticate with.
  -T [ --jwt-token ] arg               Explicit JWT token. Used as-is.
  -k [ --jwt-secret ] arg              JWT Signing Key. Uses Basic 
                                       Authentication if omitted.
  --no-http-headers                    Use URL for AuthN. Emulates 
                                       Browser-based clients.

OSDU Partition Options:
  -P [ --data-partition-id ] arg       OSDU data partition name.

Info: openETPServer: done.
